<article class="env-lemma" id="05D0">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/05D0">Lemma <span data-tag="05D0">10.91.3</span>.</a> Let $R$ be a Noetherian ring and $A$ a set. Then $M = R^ A$ is a flat and Mittag-Leffler $R$-module. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Combining Lemma <a href="/tag/05CY" data-tag="05CY">10.90.5</a> and Proposition <a href="/tag/05CZ" data-tag="05CZ">10.90.6</a> we see that $M$ is flat over $R$. We show that $M$ satisfies the condition of Lemma <a href="/tag/059S" data-tag="059S">10.91.2</a>. Let $F$ be a free finite $R$-module. If $F'$ is any submodule of $F$ then it is finitely presented since $R$ is Noetherian. So by Proposition <a href="/tag/059K" data-tag="059K">10.89.3</a> we have a commutative diagram 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ F' \otimes _ R M \ar[r] \ar[d]^{\cong } &  F \otimes _ R M \ar[d]^{\cong } \\  (F')^ A \ar[r] &  F^ A }  \]
</div>
    <p>
       by which we can identify the map $F' \otimes _ R M \to F \otimes _ R M$ with $(F')^ A \to F^ A$. Hence if $x \in F \otimes _ R M$ corresponds to $(x_\alpha ) \in F^ A$, then the submodule of $F'$ of $F$ generated by the $x_\alpha $ is the smallest submodule of $F$ such that $x \in F' \otimes _ R M$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>